prerequisites produced content drift in committed derived artifacts:
`experiments/derived/arm1_flat/mistral_run0{1..5}.md` (+~28 lines each)
and `experiments/derived/sota_cross_eval.csv` (~32 lines changed). The
committed artifacts predate the current extractor code. The drift was
deliberately NOT committed in #990 (kept that PR Makefile-only).

Note: PR #994 (ticket 0292) subsequently changed the extractors again
(citation resolution, preamble strip, audit sidecars) — regenerate
after it lands and diagnose against THAT code state.

## Actions
1. Regenerate arm1-4 flat dirs + sota_cross_eval.csv from current code.
2. Diagnose the diff: legitimate extractor evolution vs nondeterminism.
3. If legitimate: commit refreshed artifacts in a data-refresh PR and
   verify downstream tables/figures that consume them.
4. If nondeterministic: isolate and fix the source first.

## Exit criteria
